{
  "info": {
    "name": "ModaCo Promotion Management API",
    "description": "Every request here runs against a stack brought up with `npm run up`.\n\nRun the folders in order: **1 Health** proves the stack is reachable, **2 Storefront** is the case study's read side, **3 Promotions** its write side, **4 Vendor import** is Scenario A, and **5 Refusals** is the validation surface — every request in that folder is expected to fail, and a 2xx there is the finding.\n\n`baseUrl` defaults to `http://127.0.0.1:3100/api`. The storefront answers 503 until the read model has been built, which the event handler does on boot.\n\nPropagation is asynchronous: a promotion reaches the storefront through a queue, not inside the request that created it. On a live stack the first product was discounted 915 ms after the 201. If a storefront assertion fails immediately after a write, run it again before believing it.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:3100/api" },
    { "key": "category", "value": "PostmanCat" },
    { "key": "productId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "promotionId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "draftId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "jobId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health — liveness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "Answers 200 even when a store is unreachable, deliberately: the compose healthcheck calls this and every worker gates on `api` being healthy, so a store-dependent health route would stop the workers that repair the system from ever starting.",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["health"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('flat ok', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ status: 'ok' }));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /ready — readiness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "Asks both stores rather than reading a flag: a pool that was built holds no connection, so nothing on this side knows a store is gone until a query fails.",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ready", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["ready"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 ready, or 503 naming what is down', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 503]);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('names both stores either way', () => {",
                  "  const d = pm.response.json().dependencies;",
                  "  pm.expect(d).to.have.property('postgres');",
                  "  pm.expect(d).to.have.property('redis');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /metrics — note the missing /api",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "Mounted at the root, outside the /api prefix and outside the error envelope, like /admin/queues.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "http://127.0.0.1:3100/metrics",
              "protocol": "http",
              "host": ["127", "0", "0", "1"],
              "port": "3100",
              "path": ["metrics"]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('prom-client default metrics', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('nodejs_heap_size_used_bytes');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2 Storefront",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /products — first page",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products?pageSize=5",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["products"],
              "query": [{ "key": "pageSize", "value": "5" }]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('the listing shape', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.all.keys('items', 'page', 'pageSize', 'total');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('every row carries an effective price, not only a base one', () => {",
                  "  body.items.forEach((p) => pm.expect(p).to.have.property('effectivePriceCents'));",
                  "});",
                  "if (body.items.length) pm.collectionVariables.set('productId', body.items[0].id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /products — sorted by effective price",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "The case study asks for sorting by the effective price. A 60 %-discounted 200.00 product sorts ahead of a 100.00 one, because the shopper pays less for it.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products?sort=effectivePrice&order=asc&pageSize=10",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["products"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "sort", "value": "effectivePrice" },
                { "key": "order", "value": "asc" },
                { "key": "pageSize", "value": "10" }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const prices = pm.response.json().items.map((p) => p.effectivePriceCents);",
                  "pm.test('ascending by what the shopper pays', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(prices).to.eql([...prices].sort((a, b) => a - b));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /products — filtered by category",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products?category=Accessories&pageSize=5",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["products"],
              "query": [
                { "key": "category", "value": "Accessories" },
                { "key": "pageSize", "value": "5" }
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('every row is in the category asked for', () => {",
                  "  pm.response.json().items.forEach((p) => pm.expect(p.category).to.eql('Accessories'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /products/:id — the busiest endpoint",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "description": "The case study calls this the most highly trafficked endpoint. It is one Redis hash read, where the listing is a sorted-set range plus a multi-get — measured at 4 375 req/s against the listing's 1 728.",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products/{{productId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["products", "{{productId}}"]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('one product with its applied promotion', () => {",
                  "  const p = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(p).to.have.property('effectivePriceCents');",
                  "  pm.expect(p).to.have.property('promotion');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3 Promotions",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /products — a product of our own",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"sku\": \"PM-{{$timestamp}}\",\n  \"name\": \"Postman product\",\n  \"category\": \"{{category}}\",\n  \"basePriceCents\": 10000,\n  \"stockQuantity\": 5\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/products", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["products"] }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
